  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southern Africa Tuberculosis and Health Systems Support Project (SATBHSS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to support the Ministry of Health Mozambique (MISAU) in developing a viable model for quality occupational health services for miners and other migrant workers, in an integrated approach that addresses patient follow-up in South Africa as well as prevention and care among communities of origin in Mozambique. This is expected to contribute to improved health outcomes of migrant workers through improving access to occupational health screening services, referral pathways, patient and relatives&#x2019; follow-up.</narrative>
  </description>
